            <Property name="rows" type="int" value="5"/>
            <Property name="text" type="java.lang.String" value="PSEUDOCODE LANGUAGE DOCUMENTATION&#xa;&#xa;1. INTRODUCTION&#xa;This document describes the custom pseudocode language supported by the interpreter. It explains the&#xa;syntax, grammar, semantics, control flow, expressions, variable rules, and examples of runnable&#xa;pseudocode programs.&#xa;&#xa;2. KEY DESIGN GOALS&#xa;- Easy to read for beginners.&#xa;- Structured like modern programming languages.&#xa;- Supports variables, expressions, arithmetic, boolean logic, conditionals, loops, and built-in functions.&#xa;- Predictable execution model defined by an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST).&#xa;&#xa;3. SYNTAX OVERVIEW&#xa;The language is line-based but supports block structures using INDENT/DEDENT or explicit&#xa;BEGIN/END depending on user preference.&#xa;Supported constructs:&#xa;- Variable assignment&#xa;- Arithmetic expressions&#xa;- Boolean expressions&#xa;- IF / ELSE&#xa;- WHILE loops&#xa;- PRINT statements&#xa;- Built-in functions&#xa;&#xa;4. VARIABLES&#xa;Variables are created automatically the first time they appear on the left-hand side of an assignment.&#xa;Syntax:&#xa;x = 10&#xa;total = a + b * 2&#xa;name = &quot;Jerian&quot;&#xa;Types supported:&#xa;- Number&#xa;- String&#xa;- Boolean (TRUE, FALSE)&#xa;&#xa;5. EXPRESSIONS&#xa;Expressions follow standard operator precedence:&#xa;Highest &#x2192; Lowest:&#xa;1. Parentheses&#xa;2. Unary: +a, -a, NOT a&#xa;3. Multiplicative: *, /, %&#xa;4. Additive: +, -&#xa;5. Comparisons: &lt;, &lt;=, &gt;, &gt;=&#xa;6. Equality: ==, !=&#xa;7. Boolean: AND, OR&#xa;Examples:&#xa;x = (a + b) * c&#xa;flag = NOT (a &gt; b)&#xa;done = counter == max OR finished == TRUE&#xa;&#xa;6. PRINTING&#xa;PRINT outputs a value to the console.&#xa;Examples:&#xa;PRINT x&#xa;PRINT &quot;Hello World&quot;&#xa;PRINT total + 10&#xa;&#xa;7. IF STATEMENTS&#xa;Syntax:&#xa;IF condition THEN&#xa;statements&#xa;ELSE&#xa;statements&#xa;ENDIF&#xa;Example:&#xa;IF score &gt;= 75 THEN&#xa;PRINT &quot;Passed&quot;&#xa;ELSE&#xa;PRINT &quot;Failed&quot;&#xa;ENDIF&#xa;&#xa;8. WHILE LOOPS&#xa;Syntax:&#xa;WHILE condition DO&#xa;statements&#xa;ENDWHILE&#xa;Example:&#xa;WHILE x &lt; 5 DO&#xa;PRINT x&#xa;x = x + 1&#xa;ENDWHILE&#xa;&#xa;9. BUILT-IN FUNCTIONS&#xa;Supported:&#xa;- INPUT() returns a string from the user.&#xa;- TO_NUMBER(x)&#xa;- TO_STRING(x)&#xa;- LENGTH(x)&#xa;- RANDOM(min, max)&#xa;Example:&#xa;name = INPUT()&#xa;PRINT LENGTH(name)&#xa;&#xa;10. FULL PROGRAM EXAMPLES&#xa;Example 1: Sum numbers 1&#x2013;5&#xa;total = 0&#xa;i = 1&#xa;WHILE i &lt;= 5 DO&#xa;total = total + i&#xa;i = i + 1&#xa;ENDWHILE&#xa;PRINT total&#xa;Example 2: Password attempt loop&#xa;password = &quot;&quot;&#xa;WHILE password != &quot;1234&quot; DO&#xa;PRINT &quot;Enter password:&quot;&#xa;password = INPUT()&#xa;ENDWHILE&#xa;PRINT &quot;Access granted&quot;&#xa;Example 3: Conditional logic&#xa;age = 20&#xa;IF age &gt;= 18 THEN&#xa;PRINT &quot;Adult&quot;&#xa;ELSE&#xa;PRINT &quot;Minor&quot;&#xa;ENDIF&#xa;END OF DOCUMENT"/>
          </Properties>
        </Component>
